abstract: >-
CCC Structural Folding Runtime (CSFR) is a general structural runtime
framework for transforming metric-space object collections into folded
Compressed Computational Cognition (CCC) structures that support runtime
dispatch, structural localization, and localized intelligence. CSFR
distinguishes object-to-object distance (D_PP), object-to-CCC distance
(D_PC), and CCC-to-CCC distance (D_CC); introduces policy-compressed
Cluster CCCs and aligned Sequence Claw-Dragon Merge; and extends runtime
search through CCC DNA, reverse structural indexing, Two-Way CCC, and
Two-Phase Structural Search. The canonical runtime progression is:
Metric -> Cluster -> Merge -> CCC -> DNA -> Retrieve -> Verify ->
Localization.

